(6090884, 893357, 117474, '<td valign="top">Hmmm. Speaking as an Irish man... that guinness looks far too see through. It should be jet black! Or is that some glare from lights/flash?</td>', 'Hmmm. Speaking as an Irish man... that guinness looks far too see through. It should be jet black! Or is that some glare from lights/flash?', '2010-07-13 15:11:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(6090902, 893357, 117285, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by NiallOTuama:</b></div><hr/><i> Hmmm. Speaking as an Irish man... that guinness looks far too see through. It should be jet black! Or is that some glare from lights/flash? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I pounded it with a flash directly behind the glass.  I know it was probably sacrilege to let the Guinness appear as anything other than jet black but I wanted to create some definition, even at the cost of it''s reputation.</td>', 'Originally posted by NiallOTuama: Hmmm. Speaking as an Irish man... that guinness looks far too see through. It should be jet black! Or is that some glare from lights/flash?   I pounded it with a flash directly behind the glass.  I know it was probably sacrilege to let the Guinness appear as anything other than jet black but I wanted to create some definition, even at the cost of it''s reputation.', '2010-07-13 15:25:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(6090914, 893357, 117474, '<td valign="top">And by the way. Good shot composure. With that shot I think it would have been very easy to make it feel very... cluttered or busy, but the eye is directed to where it''s supposed to be. It goes over the rest of it as an afterthought, and there''s a good atmosphere in the background too.<br/> <br/>Now that you said you pounded it with the flash I notice the bright areas near the bottom of the shot. <br/> <br/>I don''t drink guinness much to be honest. I''m more of a <a href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beamish_Stout#Beamish_stout" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">beamish</a> man. I''m surprised the light penetrated the drink! Failing that I''d go for <a href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Murphy''s_Irish_Stout" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Murphy''s</a>. Then Guinness. <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-07-13 14:40:18.</i></td>', 'And by the way. Good shot composure. With that shot I think it would have been very easy to make it feel very... cluttered or busy, but the eye is directed to where it''s supposed to be. It goes over the rest of it as an afterthought, and there''s a good atmosphere in the background too. Now that you said you pounded it with the flash I notice the bright areas near the bottom of the shot.  I don''t drink guinness much to be honest. I''m more of a beamish man. I''m surprised the light penetrated the drink! Failing that I''d go for Murphy''s. Then Guinness. ', '2010-07-13 15:38:33.000000', '2010-07-13 15:40:18.000000', 0),
(6092649, 893221, 29011, '<td valign="top">Such a lovely and delicate capture. I''m so glad you''re happy and doing well. Congrats on the ribbon and on the courage you had to give those wings a chance :)</td>', 'Such a lovely and delicate capture. I''m so glad you''re happy and doing well. Congrats on the ribbon and on the courage you had to give those wings a chance :)', '2010-07-14 12:48:17.000000', NULL, 0),
